lo/src/render/svg.ts\n@@ -441,7 +441,7 @@ function updatePath(n: SvgNode, mark: PathMark, bindings: PaintBindings): void {\n }\n \n function updateBars(doc: Document, g: SvgNode, mark: RectMark, bindings: PaintBindings, pattern: string | null): void {\n-  // The group carries the color; each <rect> is painted on its own, so overlaps composite like canvas.\n+  // The group carries the color; each <rect> is painted on its own so overlaps composite.\n   // With a pattern, every rectangle is repeated once more, filled with the pattern, after all the fills.\n   paint(g, 'fill', paintOf(mark.fill, bindings));\n   const q = mark.xywh;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat AGENTS.md; rg -n '\"'^#{1,5} |render|Renderer|benchmark|performance|mark|artifact|sealed'\"' docs/02-product-spec.md docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat AGENTS.md; rg -n '\"'^#{1,5} |render|Renderer|benchmark|performance|mark|artifact|sealed'\"' docs/02-product-spec.md docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Working in this repository\n\nAxylo is a browser charting library. The product is specified in `docs/02-product-spec.md`; the build plan is `docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md`. Read the sections your task names before writing code.\n\n## Rules for every change\n\n- **Contracts are fixed.** `packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts` and `packages/axylo/src/public.ts` are the interfaces between modules. Do not edit them. If your work needs a change there, stop that part, finish what you can, and describe the exact change you need in your report.\n- **Stay in your files.** Each task lists the directories it owns. Do not create, edit or delete anything else, including configuration and other modules. Several agents work in this checkout at the same time.\n- **No runtime dependencies.** Use the platform (`Intl`, typed arrays). Dev dependencies already installed: TypeScript, Vitest, fast-check, esbuild, Playwright (system Chrome), axe-core. The network is not available; do not try to install anything.\n- **No DOM at import time.** A module that needs the DOM takes it as a parameter or touches it inside a function. Pure stages (data, scales, formatting, layout, scene) must run in Node.\n- **Hot paths use typed arrays.** No object per data point, no array of arrays per data point, no copying of large columns that the contracts say are borrowed.\n- **Never guess silently.** Anything that cannot be drawn as given is reported through the `DiagnosticSink` with the code from spec section 3.5.\n- **Tests come from the spec.** Expected values are derived from the specification and the fixture data, never by running the implementation and pasting its output. Use fast-check property tests for invariants (\"for any data …\"). A test you cannot make pass is reported as failing; do not weaken it or change its expected value.\n- **TypeScript strict, no `any`** in exported signatures. `__DEV__` is a build-time boolean (true in tests).\n- **Comments say why**, not what. Names are plain words.\n- **Do not commit.** The coordinator commits.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\nnpm run typecheck      # tsc over the library, its tests, and the API examples in docs/api\nnpm test               # unit and property tests (Node)\nnpm run build          # packages/axylo/dist\nnpm run test:browser   # browser tests against the built bundle, in system Chrome\n```\n\n## Your report\n\nEnd with a short report: what you built (files), what you verified and how (paste the last lines of the test run), what is not done or not verified, any contract change you need, and any place where the spec was ambiguous and what you assumed. Keep \"ran and saw\" apart from \"expect\".\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:1:# Phase 2 plan: Axylo 1.0 in TypeScript\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:3:Revision 3, 2026-11-18. Revised after three independent reviews ([ledger](../reviews/2026-11-18/ledger.md)) and the owner's decisions of the same day (scatter and a compact variant are in 1.0; the mark renderer is decided in M1).\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:7:**The release is done when every row of the acceptance matrix passes.** The matrix lives in the repository as data: one row per spec criterion and chart type, naming the test that covers it, with a result of pass, fail or not applicable (with the reason). The Phase 1 comparison is rerun with Axylo included and published, but it is comparison evidence, not the gate: several of its columns are descriptive, and it cannot run the performance budgets.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:9:## 1. Public API\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:13:### 1.1 Shape\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:38:### 1.2 Data: one logical table, three forms\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:63:### 1.3 Fields\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:90:### 1.4 Common options\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:100:| `compact` | Line, area and bar: marks only, as a static image with a text alternative (spec 3.7). |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:107:### 1.5 Handle and commit contract\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:130:### 1.6 Diagnostics\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:145:`validate(type, options)` runs the same normalization without a DOM and returns the diagnostics, so a server, a test or a coding agent can check a chart before rendering it.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:149:### 1.7 React adapter (not in 1.0)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:161:| Lifecycle | Create on mount, `destroy` on unmount; correct under StrictMode's setup, cleanup, setup. The file is marked `'use client'`. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:162:| Props to options | Field specs are compared structurally, so an inline `x={{ field: 'ts' }}` does not renormalize on every render. `data` is compared by identity; in development, the same content arriving three times with a new identity raises a hint to memoize it. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:169:## 2. Architecture\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:171:### 2.1 Pipeline\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:174:options ─► normalize ─► frame ──┬─► view model ─► layout ─► scene ─► mark renderer\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:175:            │ validate   (authoritative) │   scales, visible range         text renderer (DOM)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:190:| renderers | Marks; DOM text; accessibility DOM | See 2.3. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:192:### 2.2 Invalidation\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:202:| mark raster | Scene; device pixel ratio; resolved colors (L4's triggers). |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:206:### 2.3 Rendering\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:208:**Working assumption: Canvas 2D for marks, HTML for all text.** Text stays in the DOM so that it inherits the page font and color, honors user text spacing and zoom (A6), adapts in forced-colors mode, and can be selected and translated.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:212:M1 builds both mark renderers behind the same scene and compares them on: P1, P2, P3, P5, bytes, memory, a runtime theme toggle, forced colors, print, and browser zoom. The scene is renderer-neutral either way, so the choice is contained.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:216:**No animation system.** First render is not animated (I5). Updates cut, or tween for at most 200 ms where the cost is negligible, and not at all under reduced motion.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:218:### 2.4 Document structure\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:226:  <div class=\"axylo-plot\" tabindex=\"0\"> … marks … <div class=\"axylo-text\" aria-hidden=\"true\">tick labels</div></div>\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:241:### 2.5 Repository\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:247:bench/                 benchmark harness (04-plan-performance.md), built in M0\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:257:## 3. Milestones\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:259:Each milestone ends with outcomes checked by a command, an example that runs in the docs site, and the documentation page for what was built. Durations are ceilings for one owner working with coding agents, not targets. Every milestone from M1 on re-runs the acceptance matrix, the size report and the benchmark smoke set, and records the results.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:261:### M0. Foundations (ceiling: 5 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:266:- The benchmark harness from the performance plan, section 3: readiness markers, main-thread accounting, the reference-machine record, and adapters for uPlot and Chart.js. It measures those two before any Axylo code exists.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:268:Outcomes: `npm test` and `npm run build` pass on three operating systems; the API report is committed; the benchmark harness reproduces a uPlot and a Chart.js measurement with a recorded noise band.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:270:### M1. A vertical slice, and the two open decisions (ceiling: 12 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:274:- **Renderer comparison:** the mark renderer built twice (Canvas 2D and SVG paths) behind the same scene, measured as in 2.3.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:279:- `trend` renders in three engines at 720 and 340 px; scene snapshot; resize in both directions with no call from the page.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:281:- Two written decision records, each with its measurements: the renderer, and the plot's interaction pattern. Each says what was observed and what was inferred.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:286:### M2. Faithful data, on the line chart (ceiling: 8 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:298:### M3. Reading the chart (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:311:### M4. Accessibility, complete on the line chart (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:324:### M5. Bar, area, donut, scatter and the compact variant (ceiling: 18 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:326:Each type is done when its column of the type matrix (spec 3.6) and every applicable row of the acceptance matrix pass, including the accessibility and performance rows. Types are finished one at a time, in this order: bar, area, donut, the compact variant, scatter.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:332:- Palette scored on rendered marks, repeats included, in both schemes; grayscale identification test.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:334:- Scatter: picking, ties, coincident points and a clustered-data benchmark.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:338:### M6. Updates and scale (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:350:### M7. Distribution and documentation (ceiling: 8 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:358:- Every runnable docs example compiled and rendered from the packed distribution (DX10).\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:361:### M8. Release (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:374:## 4. Test strategy\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:390:## 5. Risks\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:402:## 6. What waits until after 1.0\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:412:| Server-side rendering to SVG | The scene makes it possible. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:417:| Public plugin or custom-mark API | After two real uses show its shape. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:419:| Workers, WebGL or WebGPU, Rust | Decided from measurements (04-plan-performance.md). |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:1:# Phase 1b: Axylo product specification\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:3:Revision 3, 2026-11-18. Revised after three independent reviews ([ledger](../reviews/2026-11-18/ledger.md)), then updated with the owner's decisions of the same day: scatter is in 1.0, a compact variant is in 1.0, and the mark renderer is decided by measurement in M1.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:5:Based on the findings in [01-landscape.md](01-landscape.md). Finding IDs (R1–R16 for readers, D1–D10 for developers) refer to that document. Criterion IDs defined here are F, L, I, A (reader), DX (developer) and P (performance).\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:7:## 1. What Axylo is\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:15:### 1.1 Why someone would choose it\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:29:### 1.2 Who it is for\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:35:### 1.3 Principles\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:42:| Everything a reader needs is on; nothing else is | Title, units, legend, tooltip, keyboard, description and table are on. Entry animation, a marker on every point of a dense line, and decorative toolbars are not. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:46:## 2. Scope of the first release\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:48:### 2.1 Chart types\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:57:| Compact variant | Of line, area and bar: marks only, for KPI tiles and sparklines | Which way is it going? | 1.0 (owner's decision) |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:65:### 2.2 Workflows\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:76:### 2.3 Supported environments\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:83:| Text direction | Left-to-right pages. Right-to-left text renders, but the layout is not mirrored; this is stated in the conformance table. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:87:## 3. Acceptance criteria: the reader's experience\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:91:### 3.1 Faithful representation\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:96:| F2 | Missing values are never drawn as zero and never bridged unless the author asks. An explicit `null` is a gap, silently. An isolated value between two gaps is a visible point. A missing bar shows a \"no data\" mark at the baseline, distinct from a zero bar; a slot a series merely has no row for gets no bar and no mark. On a time or date axis with a regular step, an absent step is a gap and raises AX105; `missing: 'zero'` on the field turns absent and null values into zeros for counts. Tooltip, table and announcements say \"No data\". | `trend` with nulls and `trend` with the same 7 rows deleted render the same gap; `dirty` fixtures; property test that no segment connects across a missing index | R5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:103:| F9 | Up to eight series, no two share a color. Beyond eight, each series still has a unique combination of color and dash or marker (for bars, full and compact alike: color and fill pattern; for every chart type at least 32 distinct combinations, after which combinations repeat), and AX130 is raised. | Tests with 6, 8 and 12 series | R7 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:104:| F10 | Stacks place positive and negative values on their own sides of zero, and the axis covers both totals. The readout's total is the sum when every component has the same sign; when signs are mixed it gives the positive total and the negative total, the two ends the reader sees, not their net. A missing component is drawn with zero height and the stack is marked \"incomplete\" in tooltip, table and announcements. A component is missing whenever its series has no value at that x, whatever the reason: a null, an absent step, or a series that simply has no row there (a weekly series stacked with a daily one is incomplete on the days between its rows; the owner's decision, 2026-11-18: a stack must never show a total made of values the data does not contain). A stacked series' line follows its band, so inside a stack it is not joined across such a slot. | Property test on stacked geometry; mixed-sign and incomplete fixtures | R5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:105:| F11 | Line, area and scatter are drawn in x order whatever the input order. On line, area and bar, two rows with the same x in one series are AX108 and that series is not drawn. On scatter, points sharing an x (or both coordinates) are ordinary data. | Shuffled `trend` renders identically; duplicate fixture | R5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:108:### 3.2 Legibility\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:113:| L2 | Text is at least 12 CSS px and at least 4.5:1 against what is behind it, including text drawn inside a mark and legend entries for hidden series. Marks, axis lines and focus indicators are at least 3:1. Gridlines are exempt: they are not needed to read a value while the tooltip and table exist. Holds in light and dark. | Computed-style and rendered-pixel checks in both schemes | R7, R10, WCAG 1.4.3, 1.4.11 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:116:| L5 | A marker on every point appears only when adjacent points are at least 12 px apart (provisional value), and always for isolated points. | `trend` at 720 px has no marker on every point (A5's sparse shape markers remain); a 12-point line has them | R8 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:121:### 3.3 Interaction\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:125:| I1 | Pointing anywhere in the plot shows what is there, by the picking rule for the chart type (section 3.6), within one frame at the 95th percentile. On line, area and bar the tooltip lists every visible series at the nearest x; a series with no row at that x reads \"No observation\", distinct from \"No data\". The tooltip stays inside the viewport, does not cover the active mark or any control, can itself be hovered, and lists at most eight rows plus \"+N more\". In a plot too small for it (decision 0004: narrower than 240 px or shorter than 140 px) the same content appears as text in a strip reserved under the plot; where even the strip would leave the plot under the minimum of L8, pointing highlights the datum without a readout and the values are in the keyboard reading and the table. Escape closes it until the pointer reaches a different datum. | Hover at 20 positions including all four edges; sparse-series fixture; narrow tile with eight series; Escape test | R15, WCAG 1.4.13, 2.4.11 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:129:| I5 | First render is not animated. An update may transition for at most 200 ms. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` nothing transitions, on first render or on update. | After `document.fonts.ready`: first frame equals the frame at 2.5 s within a 0.1% pixel tolerance, in both settings; an update under reduced motion reaches its final frame in one step; a 24-chart filter change settles within 200 ms | R14 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:132:### 3.4 Accessibility\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:134:Target: every WCAG 2.2 level AA success criterion that applies to what Axylo renders, as component-level evidence. Conformance of a page is a property of the page and remains the author's.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:142:| A5 | Series are never distinguished by color alone, in any mode. Each line and area carries a shape marker at its last point and at sparse intervals, repeated in the legend and tooltip; under `prefers-contrast: more` or forced colors, lines also differ by dash. Adjacent filled marks (slices, stacked segments) are separated by at least 1 px of background. Bars are told apart by position and order, and by the legend and tooltip that name them; a compact chart has neither, so there neighbouring bar series also differ by fill pattern (series further apart may share a pattern: four patterns exist). The default palette has eight colors, each at least 3:1 on the default light and dark backgrounds, with a minimum pairwise OKLab difference of 0.10 (provisional) under normal vision and simulated protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. On any other background, Axylo measures the palette against the resolved background and raises AX141 below 3:1. | Palette script scoring the rendered marks of an eight-series chart in both schemes, repeats included; rendered-pixel checks of separators; a grayscale screenshot in which three crossing lines can be told apart by marker | R7, WCAG 1.4.1, 1.4.11 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:147:| A10 | Every built-in string can be replaced through `messages`. Built-in English text is marked `lang=\"en\"` when the document language is not English. | Test on a `lang=\"de\"` page | WCAG 3.1.2 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:149:### 3.5 Diagnostic registry\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:170:| AX130 | Warning | More than eight series | All series, with dash or marker differences |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:189:### 3.6 Type matrix\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:201:### 3.7 Compact variant\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:203:`compact: true` on line, area and bar draws the marks and nothing else: no axes, gridlines, legend, toolbar, table control, zoom or tooltip. It is for a small tile where the page already shows the number and the label.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:211:| C5 | When values were left out (F12), the description says so and a small marker with a text equivalent appears in the corner. | `dirty` fixture in compact mode, WCAG 1.1.1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:215:### 3.8 What the evidence will and will not show\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:219:## 4. Acceptance criteria: the developer's experience\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:223:| DX1 | The first chart takes ten lines or fewer, including import, by npm and by script tag. No required option besides data and fields. | Two CI tests that render the documented snippet from the packed distribution | D1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:225:| DX3 | With typed rows, a misspelled field, a text field on a value axis, wide `y` combined with `series`, and an option that does not apply to the chart type all fail to compile. At run time, for untyped rows, the same mistakes raise AX101, AX106 and AX150. | [docs/api/examples.ts](api/examples.ts) compiles and each marked mistake fails (already checked with TypeScript 7.0.2); runtime tests per code | D5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:227:| DX5 | Three methods change a chart: `update` changes options, `append` adds rows, `zoom` sets the view. They apply in call order. Validation and diagnostics are synchronous; drawing is deferred to the next frame; marks, labels, hit testing and the accessibility layer always switch to a new state together. `destroy()` releases everything and cancels pending work. No `resize()` exists. | Sequence tests: replace then append then zoom in one turn; a rejected `strict` update leaves the last valid chart; destroy before the frame; 1,000 create–destroy cycles show no heap growth trend (P7) | D3, R16 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:232:| DX10 | Every runnable example in the documentation is compiled and rendered in CI from the packed distribution. | Docs build | D1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:236:## 5. Performance budgets\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:238:These numbers are provisional. They are design targets taken from Phase 1's order-of-magnitude measurements, and they become release gates only after the benchmark harness built in M0 has measured a working Axylo slice in M1 and the limits have been recalibrated and frozen (plan, M1 and M6). Each budget names its workload, metric and statistic so that two people measuring the same build get the same verdict.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:257:## 6. Decisions and the findings behind them\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:267:| No animation on first render | Reading starts at first paint, and with 24 charts loading at once motion competes with it. R14: four of seven animating libraries ignore reduced motion. | Kept, with the rationale restated. Update transitions stay capped at 200 ms. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:271:| SVG marks with DOM text | The two renderers were built on the same scene and measured. | The owner chose SVG as the only mark renderer for 1.0 on 2026-11-22. See [decision 0002](decisions/0002-mark-renderer.md). |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:273:| Palette held to measurable thresholds | R7. | Kept as a screen, marked provisional. Marks carry a non-color cue in every mode, which the first draft did not require. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:282:## 7. Changes this revision rejected\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:291:## 8. Decisions still open\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:293:The owner included scatter and the compact variant on 2026-11-18 and chose SVG as the only 1.0 mark renderer on 2026-11-22.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
