r loading and the readback are outside.\n355:includes dispatch, append, the chart's work and the harness's tracking. `lateFrames` = frame intervals later than\n373:by name. The count excludes the caller's typed columns and canvas backing stores. The harness records the total as\n434:whose harness files (page, adapters) differ, so only the library differs. `--screen --tolerance <t>` applies the\n465:## What the harness needs from the library\n7:## 1. What Phase 1 established, and what it did not\n18:## 2. Workloads\n39:## 3. How to measure\n41:### 3.1 Metrics\n59:### 3.2 Environment\n72:### 3.3 Statistics\n82:### 3.4 Comparison libraries\n98:## 4. The improvement loop\n124:## 5. What makes a gain worth shipping\n139:### 5.1 Declared endpoints (provisional until the pilot)\n173:## 6. Catching regressions\n187:## 7. Where Rust could be justified, and what it would take\n191:### 7.1 Candidates\n204:### 7.2 Preconditions for starting\n211:### 7.3 Evidence required to adopt\n227:### 7.4 Decision\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
